nss_coredump: allow dumping the firmware log ring on demand

The firmware's log ring is only ever printed from the coredump path,
which runs when the firmware signals a crash. A firmware that is wedged
rather than crashed never signals, so its log - the only first-hand
account of what it was doing - stays unread.

The ring is host memory (meminfo debug_boot_log_desc), so walking it
needs nothing from the firmware. Split the walk out of
nss_fw_coredump_notify() and add sysctl dev.nss.general.fwlog to run it
on demand, without marking the core dead or arming the panic path.

Used to diagnose the wifili start wedging the phys_if node on IPQ5018.

